Package: reboot-when-idle
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: all
Maintainer: Gooder24 <162874774+Gooder24@users.noreply.github.com>
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Depends: systemd, procps, iproute2, mawk | awk
Recommends: unattended-upgrades, grub-common
Description: reboot after updates, but only while nothing works on the machine
 Made for machines that run AI coding agents unattended. A nightly timer
 reboots when a newer kernel is installed, a package asked for it or the
 machine has been up for a month - and only when no agent turn, agent command,
 held job, apt run or typing is under way. Claude Code hooks tell it when an
 agent works; "reboot-when-idle hold <command>" covers anything else. A new
 kernel is started once on trial: without network, after a crash or a hang the
 machine goes back to the kernel that worked.
